# undo goes back to the previous revision: its ReplicaSet is scaled up again and renumbered 4.
$ kubectl rollout undo deployment/web
deployment.apps/web rolled back
$ kubectl rollout status deployment/web
Waiting for deployment spec update to be observed...
Waiting for deployment spec update to be observed...
Waiting for deployment "web" rollout to finish: 1 old replicas are pending termination...
deployment "web" successfully rolled out
$ kubectl rollout history deployment/web
deployment.apps/web 
REVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE
1         <none>
3         try nginx 9.99
4         upgrade to nginx 1.28

$ kubectl get deployment web -o yaml | grep -e image: -e change-cause
    kubernetes.io/change-cause: upgrade to nginx 1.28
      - image: nginx:1.28
# restart changes only the restartedAt annotation of the template: a new ReplicaSet, same image.
